Here's an example implementation of the `formatCSS` function:
```javascript
function formatCSS(styleRules) {
  let css = '';

  for (const selector in styleRules) {
    const properties = styleRules[selector];
    if (!properties) continue;

    css += `${selector} {`;

    for (const property in properties) {
      const value = properties[property];
      if (value !== undefined && value !== null) {
        css += `  ${property}: ${value};`;
      }
    }

    css += '}\n';
  }

  return css;
}
```
This function iterates over the `styleRules` object and builds a string of CSS rules. For each selector, it checks if there are any associated style properties, and if so, it formats them as CSS properties using the `property: value;` syntax. The resulting string is then returned.

