Here's an example of how you could implement this functionality in PHP:
```php
function validatePassword($password) {
  // Check if password length is at least 8 characters
  if (strlen($password) < 8) {
    return false;
  }

  // Check if password contains at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one digit, and one special character
  $uppercase = preg_match('/[A-Z]/', $password);
  $lowercase = preg_match('/[a-z]/', $password);
  $digit = preg_match('/\d/', $password);
  $special = preg_match('/[!, @, #, $, %, ^, &, *]/', $password);
  if ($uppercase && $lowercase && $digit && $special) {
    return true;
  } else {
    return false;
  }
}
```
You can then use this function in your web form to validate the password input:
```php
