Here is an example of how you can create a class in Python to represent a car and include methods to set and get the car's color, model, and year:
```
class Car:
    def __init__(self, color, model, year):
        self.color = color
        self.model = model
        self.year = year

    @property
    def color(self):
        return self._color

    @color.setter
    def color(self, value):
        self._color = value

    @property
    def model(self):
        return self._model

    @model.setter
    def model(self, value):
        self._model = value

    @property
    def year(self):
        return self._year

    @year.setter
    def year(self, value):
        self._year = value

    def accelerate(self, acceleration):
        if self.speed + acceleration <= 300:
            self.speed += acceleration
        else:
            print("Maximum speed limit exceeded!")

    def decelerate(self, deceleration):
        if self.speed - deceleration >= -50:
            self.speed -= deceleration
        else:
            print("Minimum speed limit exceeded!")
```
This class includes three methods to set and get the car's color, model, and year, as well as two methods called "accelerate" and "decelerate". The "accelerate" method increases the car's speed by a given value, while the "decelerate" method decreases the car's speed by a given value.

The "accelerate" method also includes a check to ensure that the car's speed does not exceed its maximum speed limit of 300 km/h. If the given acceleration value exceeds this limit, the car's speed is set to the maximum limit.

Similarly, the "decelerate" method includes a check to ensure that the car's speed does not go below -50 km/h. If the given deceleration value exceeds the car's current speed, the car's speed is set to -50 km/h.

Note that this class also includes two decorators `@property` and `@color.setter`, which are used to define a getter and setter method for the `color` attribute. These decorators allow you to access and modify the color of the car using the `car.color` syntax, while ensuring that the color is always validated as a string value.

