```
def find_pair(numbers, target):
    pairs = []
    for i in range(len(numbers)):
        for j in range(i+1, len(numbers)):
            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == target:
                pairs.append((numbers[i], numbers[j]))
    return pairs
```
This function uses two nested loops to iterate over the array of numbers and find pairs that sum up to the target value. If a pair is found, it is appended to the list of pairs. After all elements have been processed, the list of pairs is returned.

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n^2), where n is the length of the array. The space complexity is O(1), as only a small amount of memory is needed to store the list of pairs.

Note that this algorithm assumes that there are no duplicates in the input array, and that there will always be at least one pair with the target sum. If there are duplicates or if no pairs exist, an empty list should be returned instead.

