            counts[elem] += 1

    # Generate the output list
    return [elem for (elem, count) in counts.items() if count > 1]
```
This solution uses a dictionary to keep track of the unique elements in the input list and their corresponding counts. It then generates the output list by iterating over the keys of the dictionary and returning only the elements that have a count greater than 1. This approach has a time complexity of O(n) because it only requires one iteration over the input list to generate the output list.

