```scss
function isOdd(n) {
  let result = '';

  while (n > 0) {
    if (n % 2 === 1) {
      result += '1';
    } else {
      result += '0';
    }
    n = Math.floor(n / 2);
  }

  return result;
}
```
This function uses a loop to check if the input number is odd or even, and appends either '1' or '0' to the result string accordingly. The loop continues until the input number is zero, at which point the result string will contain the binary representation of the input number.

