The efficient Quicksort algorithm can be designed to sort an array of positive and negative integer values by first sorting the array into two sub-arrays, one containing only positive integers and another containing only negative integers. This can be done by iterating through the array and separating each element based on its sign (positive or negative). After separating the elements, the sorted arrays can be merged together to form a single sorted array.

Here is an example of how this could be implemented:
```
function sortArray(arr) {
  // Separate positive and negative integers
  let posArr = [];
  let negArr = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > 0) {
      posArr.push(arr[i]);
    } else {
      negArr.push(arr[i]);
    }
  }

  // Sort the positive integers in ascending order
  posArr = quickSort(posArr);

  // Sort the negative integers in descending order
  negArr = quickSort(negArr).reverse();

  // Merge the sorted arrays
  return [...posArr, ...negArr];
}
```
The `quickSort` function is a divide-and-conquer algorithm that sorts an array of numbers recursively. It works by selecting a pivot element from the array and partitioning it into two sub-arrays based on whether the elements are less than or greater than the pivot. The function then recursively sorts each sub-array until the entire array is sorted.

The `reverse` method is used to reverse the order of the negative integers in descending order.

Here is an example of how the `quickSort` function could be implemented:
```
function quickSort(arr) {
  if (arr.length <= 1) {
    return arr;
  }

  // Select a pivot element from the array
  let pivot = arr[0];

  // Partition the array into two sub-arrays
  let lessThanPivot = [];
  let greaterThanPivot = [];
  for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] < pivot) {
      lessThanPivot.push(arr[i]);
    } else {
      greaterThanPivot.push(arr[i]);
    }
  }

  // Recursively sort each sub-array
  let sortedLessThanPivot = quickSort(lessThanPivot);
  let sortedGreaterThanPivot = quickSort(greaterThanPivot);

  // Merge the sorted arrays
  return [...sortedLessThanPivot, pivot, ...sortedGreaterThanPivot];
}
```
The `sortArray` function takes an array of integers as input and sorts it using the `quickSort` function. It first separates the elements into positive and negative integers, sorts each sub-array separately using `quickSort`, and then merges the sorted arrays together to form a single sorted array.

