To correct this issue, we can modify the code as follows:
```python
def sort_list(arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)):
        min_index = i
        for j in range(i+1, len(arr)):
            if arr[j] < arr[min_index]:
                min_index = j
        if min_index != i:
            arr[i], arr[min_index] = arr[min_index], arr[i]
    return arr
```
In the corrected code, we added an extra check to ensure that we only swap elements at `arr[i]` and `arr[min_index]` if they are not in their correct positions. This ensures that the algorithm does not unnecessarily swap elements that are already in their correct position.

The time complexity of this corrected code is O(n^2), as it has two nested loops with a linear time complexity inside them. The space complexity is also O(1), as no extra memory is allocated for the sorting process.

function triangleArea(a, b, c) {
