To find the minimum element in a sorted rotated array, we can use the following approach:

1. Check if the first element is the minimum. If it is not, then there must be a smaller element in the array.
2. Check if the last element is the minimum. If it is not, then there must be a smaller element in the array.
3. If neither of the above conditions are true, then the minimum element must be in the middle of the array.

