public int findMin(int[] arr) {
    if (arr[0] < arr[arr.length - 1]) {
        return arr[0];
    } else if (arr[arr.length - 1] < arr[0]) {
        return arr[arr.length - 1];
    } else {
        int min = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
            if (arr[i] < min) {
                min = arr[i];
            }
        }
        return min;
    }
}
```
This algorithm has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the array. It works by checking each element in the array until it finds the minimum element, which is either the first element or the last element if neither are the minimum, or the smallest element in the middle of the array if both are not the minimum.

