class Node:
    def __init__(self, value):
        self.value = value
        self.left = None
        self.right = None

def dfs(root):
    stack = [root]
    visited = set()
    result = []

    while stack:
        node = stack.pop()
        if node not in visited:
            visited.add(node)
            if node.left:
                stack.append(node.left)
            if node.right:
                stack.append(node.right)
            result.append(node.value)

    return result
```
This implementation uses a stack to keep track of the nodes that need to be visited, and a set to keep track of the nodes that have already been visited. The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of nodes in the tree, because each node is only visited once. The space complexity is O(h), where h is the height of the tree, because the stack can grow up to the height of the tree and the set uses O(h) memory. This implementation does not use recursion or any additional data structures, which are the requirements of the question.

