$f_terms = get_terms_by_initial($array, 'f');
```
This will return two arrays: `$e_terms` and `$f_terms`, each containing the terms from the original array that start with the specified initial character.

Here is a PHP function that extracts all terms commencing with a specified alphabetical character from a provided array, including handling uppercase characters and non-alphabetic starting characters:
```php
function extract_terms_starting_with($array, $initial) {
  // Convert the initial character to lowercase for case insensitive matching
  $lowercase_initial = strtolower($initial);

  // Initialize an empty array to store the extracted terms
  $extracted_terms = array();

  // Loop through each term in the provided array
  foreach ($array as $term) {
    // Convert the current term to lowercase for case insensitive matching
    $lowercase_term = strtolower($term);

    // Check if the term starts with the designated initial character
    if (strpos($lowercase_term, $lowercase_initial) === 0) {
      // Add the term to the extracted terms array
      $extracted_terms[] = $term;
    }
  }

  return $extracted_terms;
}
```
To use this function, you can call it with the following code:
```php
$array = ["Apple", "ball", "Cat", "dart", "Elephant", "!fun", "_goat"];
$initial = "e";
$extracted_terms = extract_terms_starting_with($array, $initial);
print_r($extracted_terms);
```
This will output the following array:
```php
Array (
  [0] => Apple
  [1] => Elephant
)
```
Note that this function uses the `strpos()` function to check if a term starts with the designated initial character. If the term starts with the initial character, it is added to the extracted terms array and returned. The `strtolower()` function is used to convert both the initial character and each term in the array to lowercase for case insensitive matching.

