We have also modified the `smallest_change` function to take into account the allowed range of integers for the modifications. If an element is within the allowed range, we skip it and do not modify it. If an element is outside the allowed range, we find the nearest element in the range and modify it. If no element in the range is found, we throw the `PalindromicVectorException`.

With these modifications, the function can now handle vectors with elements that are not within the allowed range of integers for the modifications, and will alert the user when a suitable modification cannot be found to make the vector palindromic.

