```
def parseURI(uri):
    components = uri.split("://")
    if len(components) == 1:
        return {"scheme": "", "host": "", "path": "", "query": {}, "fragment": ""}
    scheme = components[0]
    rest = components[1]
    host_path = rest.split("/", 2)
    if len(host_path) == 1:
        return {"scheme": scheme, "host": host_path[0], "path": "", "query": {}, "fragment": ""}
    host = host_path[0]
    path = "/" + host_path[1]
    query_fragment = rest.split("#", 1)
    if len(query_fragment) == 1:
        return {"scheme": scheme, "host": host, "path": path, "query": {}, "fragment": ""}
    query = query_fragment[0].split("?")
    if len(query) == 1:
        return {"scheme": scheme, "host": host, "path": path, "query": {}, "fragment": query_fragment[1]}
    query = {q.split("=")[0]: q.split("=")[1] for q in query[1].split("&")}
    return {"scheme": scheme, "host": host, "path": path, "query": query, "fragment": query_fragment[1]}
```

This function uses string splitting and slicing to extract the different components of a URI. It first splits the input URI on the "://" separator to get the scheme and the rest of the URI. If there is no separator, it means that the URI has no scheme, so an empty dictionary is returned.

The function then splits the rest of the URI on "/" to get the host and the path. If there are fewer than two slashes, it means that the URI has no path, so an empty string is returned.

Next, the function splits the query parameters and fragment from the rest of the URI using the "#" separator. If there are fewer than two hash marks, it means that the URI has no query parameters or fragment, so an empty dictionary and an empty string are returned, respectively.

The function then uses a list comprehension to create a dictionary containing the key-value pairs of the query parameters. It first splits each query parameter on "=" to get the key and value, and then uses a dictionary comprehension to create a dictionary with the key-value pairs.

Finally, the function returns a dictionary containing all the extracted components of the URI.

