To validate whether a two-dimensional array of integers represents a palindromic sequence both row-wise and column-wise, we can follow these steps:

1. Check if the array has an odd length when combined row-wise or column-wise.
2. Check if the elements in each row are equal to their mirror image in the reverse row.
3. Check if the elements in each column are equal to their mirror image in the reverse column.

Here's an example implementation of the algorithm:
```scss
function validatePalindrome(arr) {
  // Step 1: Check if the array has an odd length when combined row-wise or column-wise
  let rowLength = arr.length;
  let colLength = arr[0].length;
  let totalLength = rowLength * colLength;
  if (totalLength % 2 == 0) {
    return false; // The array has an even length, which means it's not a palindrome
  }

  // Step 2: Check if the elements in each row are equal to their mirror image in the reverse row
  for (let i = 0; i < rowLength; i++) {
    let reverseRow = arr[i].reverse();
    for (let j = 0; j < colLength; j++) {
      if (arr[i][j] !== reverseRow[j]) {
        return false; // The elements in the row are not equal to their mirror image
      }
    }
  }

  // Step 3: Check if the elements in each column are equal to their mirror image in the reverse column
  for (let i = 0; i < colLength; i++) {
    let reverseCol = [];
    for (let j = 0; j < rowLength; j++) {
      reverseCol.push(arr[j][i]);
    }
    for (let j = 0; j < rowLength; j++) {
      if (arr[j][i] !== reverseCol[j]) {
        return false; // The elements in the column are not equal to their mirror image
      }
    }
  }

  return true; // All checks passed, the array is a palindrome
}
```
This algorithm performs all checks in-place, meaning it doesn't use any additional data structures. It first checks if the array has an odd length when combined row-wise or column-wise, and if not, returns false immediately. If the array does have an odd length, it then checks if each row is equal to its mirror image in the reverse row using a nested loop. Finally, it checks if each column is equal to its mirror image in the reverse column using another nested loop.

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n^2), where n is the number of rows in the array. The space complexity is also O(1), since no additional data structures are used.

