public class FileUtils {
    /**
     * Reads the contents of a file as a string.
     */
    public static String readFile(String fileName) throws IOException {
        // Open the file and create an input stream
        FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(fileName);
        InputStreamReader isr = new InputStreamReader(fis, "UTF-8");
        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(isr);

        // Read the contents of the file into a string builder
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        String line;
        while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
            sb.append(line + "\n");
        }

        // Close the input stream and return the string
        isr.close();
        fis.close();
        return sb.toString();
    }

    /**
     * Writes a string to a file, overwriting any existing content.
     */
    public static void writeFile(String fileName, String contents) throws IOException {
        // Open the file and create an output stream
        FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(fileName);
        OutputStreamWriter osw = new OutputStreamWriter(fos, "UTF-8");
        BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(osw);

        // Write the contents of the string to the file
        bw.write(contents);
        bw.flush();

        // Close the output stream and return
        osw.close();
        fos.close();
    }

    /**
     * Appends a string to a file, creating it if it doesn't exist.
     */
    public static void appendFile(String fileName, String contents) throws IOException {
        // Open the file and create an output stream
        FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream(fileName, true);
        OutputStreamWriter osw = new OutputStreamWriter(fos, "UTF-8");
        BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(osw);

        // Write the contents of the string to the file
        bw.write(contents);
        bw.flush();

        // Close the output stream and return
        osw.close();
        fos.close();
    }
}
```
This class provides utility methods for reading and writing files as strings. The `readFile` method reads the contents of a file into a string, while the `writeFile` method writes a string to a file overwriting any existing content. The `appendFile` method appends a string to a file, creating it if it doesn't exist.

