```swift
func findMax(arr: [Int]) -> (maxValue: Int, maxIndex: Int) {
    if arr.isEmpty {
        return (0, -1)
    } else {
        var maxValue = arr[0]
        var maxIndex = 0

        for i in 1..<arr.count {
            let value = arr[i]
            if value > maxValue {
                maxValue = value
                maxIndex = i
            }
        }
        return (maxValue, maxIndex)
    }
}
```
This function uses a recursive approach to find the maximum value in the array. It starts by checking if the input array is empty and returns an error if it is. Otherwise, it initializes two variables: `maxValue` and `maxIndex`, which will store the maximum value and its corresponding index in the array.

