You are correct, my previous response was not optimal in terms of efficiency. Here's an optimized version of the code that breaks the loop as soon as the matrix is filled:
```scss
function generateMatrix(n) {
  let matrix = new Array(n).fill().map(() => new Array(n));
  let i = 0, j = 0;
  for (let row = 0; row < n; row++) {
    for (let col = 0; col < n; col++) {
      matrix[row][col] = i * n + j + 1;
      if (++j === n) {
        j = 0;
        ++i;
      }
    }
  }
  return matrix;
}
```
This implementation is more efficient because it avoids the unnecessary iterations that were present in the previous version. The `fill()` method is used to initialize the matrix with empty arrays, and then the loop fills the array with the correct values using the `++i` and `++j` variables to keep track of the row and column indices.

