```javascript
function validateForm() {
  var name = document.forms["myForm"]["name"].value;
  var email = document.forms["myForm"]["email"].value;
  var message = document.forms["myForm"]["message"].value;

  if (name == "" || email == "" || message == "") {
    alert("Please fill in all the fields");
    return false;
  }

  // Sanitize user input to prevent XSS attacks
  name = sanitize(name);
  email = sanitize(email);
  message = sanitize(message);

  var data = {
    "name": name,
    "email": email,
    "message": message
  };

  // Send the data to the server using fetch API
  fetch("https://your-server.com/api/sendMessage", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(data)
  })
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => console.log("Message sent successfully"))
  .catch(error => console.log("Error sending message:", error));

  // Clear the form fields after submission
  document.forms["myForm"]["name"].value = "";
  document.forms["myForm"]["email"].value = "";
  document.forms["myForm"]["message"].value = "";
}

function sanitize(str) {
  // Use a safe subset of HTML entities to prevent XSS attacks
  return str.replace(/[&<>"'`]/g, function (s) {
    return "&#" + s.charCodeAt(0) + ";";
  });
}
```
This updated code includes the following changes:

* The `sanitize` function is added to sanitize user input to prevent XSS attacks. This function replaces certain characters with their corresponding HTML entities.
* The `validateForm` function checks if all the form fields have been filled in before sending the data to the server. If any of the fields are empty, it will display an alert message and not send the data.
* The `sanitize` function is called on each field value before sending the data to the server. This ensures that any special characters or malicious code in the user input is removed.
* The `fetch` API is used to send the data to the server instead of using `XMLHttpRequest`. This is a more modern and secure way of making HTTP requests.
* The `JSON.stringify` method is used to convert the form data into a JSON object before sending it to the server. This ensures that the data is sent in a structured format that can be easily parsed by the server.
* The `then` method is used to handle the response from the server after the data has been sent. In this example, we log the message "Message sent successfully" if the request was successful and log any errors if there were problems with the request.
* Finally, we clear the form fields after submission using the `value` property set to an empty string. This ensures that the form is reset after each submission.

